---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "How to Choose a Personal Injury Attorney",
      "description": "Key factors to evaluate when hiring a PI attorney - experience, fee structure, communication, and how to verify bar credentials.",
      "datePublished": "2026-08-15",
      "dateModified": "2026-08-16",
      "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Personal Injury Attorney Directory" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.findpiattorney.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "How to Choose a PI Attorney", "item": "https://www.findpiattorney.com/how-to-choose-a-pi-attorney/" }
      ]
    }
  ]
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Choose a Personal Injury Attorney | PI Directory"
  description="A practical guide to evaluating and hiring the right PI attorney - experience, contingency fees, communication, bar verification, and red flags to avoid."
  canonical="https://www.findpiattorney.com/how-to-choose-a-pi-attorney/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1">

    <!-- Hero with background image -->
    <section class="relative text-white overflow-hidden bg-brand-900">
      <img
        src="/images/legal-banner.webp"
        alt="Abstract legal pattern with scales of justice, courthouse columns, and law books"
        class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
        loading="eager"
        width="1024"
        height="1024"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-brand-900/70"></div>
      <div class="relative page-container py-10 sm:py-14">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">How to Choose a Personal Injury Attorney</h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-2 mb-1">Updated: August 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-200 max-w-2xl">A practical checklist for evaluating PI attorneys - before you sign anything.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="page-container section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-10">

        <!-- Disclaimer -->
        <div class="p-4 bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-400 rounded-r-xl text-sm text-gray-700">
          <p class="font-bold text-amber-900 mb-1">Educational Information Only</p>
          <p>This page provides general guidance. It is not legal advice. Consult a licensed attorney about your specific situation.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Intro -->
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          The attorney you choose will be your advocate through negotiations, filings, depositions, and potentially a trial. That makes this decision consequential. Here's a practical framework for evaluating your options - and the red flags to watch for.
        </p>

        <!-- Step 1: Bar verification -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">1</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Verify Bar Membership First</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Before anything else, confirm the attorney holds an active license in your state. You can verify using:</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
            <div class="bg-brand-50 border border-brand-100 rounded-xl p-4 text-sm">
              <p class="font-bold text-brand-900 mb-1">This Directory</p>
              <p class="text-gray-600">Bar number and status shown on every attorney profile.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-sm">
              <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">State Bar Website</p>
              <p class="text-gray-600">Search by name or bar number for current license status and any disciplinary history.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600">Look for <strong>"Member in Good Standing / Eligible to Practice"</strong>. Avoid any status showing "Inactive," "Delinquent," or disciplinary notation.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2: Experience -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">2</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Prioritize Personal Injury Experience</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">PI law is specialized. A general practitioner who also handles divorces, real estate, and criminal defense may not be equipped for complex injury litigation. Look for attorneys who:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {[
              "Focus specifically on personal injury or plaintiff's tort law",
              "Have experience with your specific case type",
              "Have handled cases against the insurers involved in your claim",
              "Are familiar with local courts and defense tactics in your area",
            ].map(item => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4 text-brand-500 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/>
                </svg>
                {item}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3: Fees -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">3</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Understand the Fee Structure</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Personal injury attorneys generally handle cases on a contingency fee basis, meaning attorney fees are contingent upon securing a settlement or court award. Fee structures and agreements vary by attorney, state bar regulations, and case complexity.</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Always request a written fee agreement before retaining an attorney. Clarify how litigation costs and case expenses are handled, whether expenses are deducted before or after fee calculations, and how client responsibility is defined under your state bar rules.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 4: Communication -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">4</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Assess Communication and Accessibility</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Poor communication is the top complaint against attorneys. During your initial consultation - usually free - assess:</p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            {[
              "Do they listen without interrupting?",
              "Do they explain clearly in plain language - not just legal jargon?",
              "Do they give a realistic assessment rather than overpromising?",
              "Will you work directly with the attorney or mostly with paralegals?",
              "How quickly do they return calls and emails?",
            ].map(q => (
              <div class="flex items-start gap-2 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-sm text-gray-700">
                <span class="text-brand-500 font-bold mt-0.5">-</span>
                {q}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 5: Track record -->
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">5</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Research Their Track Record</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Past results don't guarantee outcomes, but a consistent track record indicates competence. Look for:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold">-</span> Client reviews on Google, Avvo, and Martindale-Hubbell</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold">-</span> Published verdicts or settlements (many firms post notable results)</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold">-</span> Peer ratings from other attorneys</li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold">-</span> State bar disciplinary history (searchable online)</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl text-sm text-red-800">
            <strong>Red flag:</strong> Any attorney who guarantees a specific outcome. This is prohibited by state bar rules and is a serious warning sign.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 6: Act quickly -->
        <div class="bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-brand-700 text-white font-bold text-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">6</span>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900">Act Quickly - Deadlines Are Hard</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Most personal injury claims have a <strong>2-year statute of limitations</strong>. But beyond the legal deadline, physical evidence degrades fast:</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
            {[
              ["Surveillance footage", "Often overwritten within 30–90 days"],
              ["Accident scene", "Conditions change quickly after the event"],
              ["Witness memory", "Fades and becomes unreliable over time"],
              ["Medical causation", "Clearest when treatment is prompt and documented"],
            ].map(([item, note]) => (
              <div class="bg-white border border-brand-100 rounded-xl px-4 py-3 text-sm">
                <p class="font-bold text-gray-900">{item}</p>
                <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs mt-0.5">{note}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- CTA -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-2xl text-center">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-900 mb-2">Find a Licensed PI Attorney</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4 text-sm">Browse licensed attorneys by state and city. Verify credentials directly with your state bar before retaining anyone.</p>
          <a href="/personal-injury-attorneys" class="btn-primary text-sm">Browse Attorneys</a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
